From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zink: A destroyed context lets go of the image it was to
 present

A context destroyed before its end-of-frame flush kept its reference to
the swapchain image waiting to be presented (needs_present), so the
swapchain outlived its window. On the PS5, whose display only one
swapchain has at a time, a game that closed a window and opened another
was then refused a swapchain for the new one. The reference now goes
with the context.

The problem and the fix are Leonardo Lobato's (prospero-win, Playden:
"fix(zink): drop a destroyed context's pending present"); this is the
same change, written for PC5's Zink at prospero-win's pin.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
index e178150..f0a711e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
@@ -133,6 +133,10 @@ zink_context_destroy(struct pipe_context *pctx)
       }
    }
 
+   /* A swapchain image still waiting for the end-of-frame flush: the context
+    * goes before it, so the swapchain must not be kept alive by it. */
+   zink_resource_reference(&ctx->needs_present, NULL);
+
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ctx->program_cache); i++) {
       simple_mtx_lock((&ctx->program_lock[i]));
       hash_table_foreach(&ctx->program_cache[i], entry) {
